        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Offerman, Gary Winick, Michael Ealy, Nora Dunn, Anne Archer, Matthew Carey, Kieran Culkin, Trieste Kelly Dunn, Martin Starr, Kevin Corrigan, Megan Mullally, Noël Wells, Stephen Root\n- Films: November, Infinity Baby, Tadpole, 13 Going on 30, Pieces of April\n- Organizations: Sundance Film Festival, NBC, InDigEnt\n- Roles: actor, voice actor, producer, writer, comedian, carpenter, director\n\nFacts:\n- Gary Winick was an American filmmaker born in 1961 and died in 2011.\n- Gary Winick directed Tadpole in 2002 and 13 Going on 30 in 2004.\n- Gary Winick produced Pieces of April in 2003 and November in 2004 through his New York City-based independent film production company InDigEnt.\n- November is a 2004 American psychological thriller film that was first screened at the 2004 Sundance Film Festival.\n- November co-stars Michael Ealy, Nora Dunn, Anne Archer, Nick Offerman, and Matthew Carey.\n- Nick Offerman was born on June 26, 1970.\n- Nick Offerman is an American actor, voice actor, producer, writer, comedian, and carpenter.\n- Nick Offerman is widely known for his breakout role as Ron Swanson in the NBC sitcom Parks and Recreation, for which he received the Television Critics Association Award for Individual Achievement in Comedy.\n- Infinity Baby stars Kieran Culkin, Trieste Kelly Dunn, Nick Offerman, Martin Starr, Kevin Corrigan, Megan Mullally, Noël Wells, and Stephen Root.",
